  "query_preview": "/Monday through Friday/...\nSouthwesterly flow aloft will still be overhead Monday as \ntroughing in the Gulf of Alaska begins to establish itself. \nThis longwave troughing pattern will become largely stationary,\ncontending with persistent upper- level ridging over the \nsouthwest CONUS. Flow aloft through the week will be out of the\nsouth/southwest, however, most of the moisture being brought\nnorth will stay west and north of the area. This combination \nwill bring mostly dry and anomalously warm conditions as the \nridge builds through the mid-week. Temperatures will climb \nrapidly from Monday onward. By Wednesday, high temperatures are \nprojected to peak in the mid to upper 60s for lower elevation \nvalleys, which is roughly 15 degrees above seasonal normals. \nSeveral locations, including the Treasure Valley, could approach\nor exceed daily record highs. Dry and tranquil conditions will \npersist across the forecast area through mid-week under this \nstrong ridge. Model guidance begins to hint at unsettled weather\napproaching late in the week / weekend as the offshore trough \nmoves slightly eastward and the ridge weakens.",
